{"duration_api_ms":280593,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"cc3598cb-5178-46bb-b1e0-5d40b8aabb22","total_cost_usd":0.7711869000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79736,"cache_read_input_tokens":399884,"output_tokens":41127,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":22076},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79736,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":25468,"cache_read_input_tokens":96318,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1740},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":7570,"outputTokens":391,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0009525000000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":363,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":41127,"cacheReadInputTokens":399884,"cacheCreationInputTokens":79736,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7702344000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":22076,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":79736,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Grep","tool_use_id":"toolu_017T9avuMxZq5PsPCJVvR9WX","tool_input":{"pattern":"\"(raw|text|value)\":","path":"C:\\Users\\isabelle\\placeholder","output_mode":"count"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer\":\"numerical_auditor\",\"paper_id\":\"bicycle-infrastructure-paper\",\"run_status\":\"ok\",\"summary\":\"Most headline numbers reconcile: the 70→36 duplicates→34 pilot funnel, the 5/8/21 coding split, the 2×2 agreement tables (33/34 = 97.1%), Table 6 (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the 44-project split (18+26), and the Table 8 listing shares (counts sum to 700,579; all shares recompute). The 35%→44% rise (about 9 pp) matches Figure 3, and the county shares in the text match Figure 4. Six defects remain. (1) The \\\"2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent)\\\" yield divides distinct openings by articles, while the paper's own counts give 5 articles. (2) \\\"Only two actual openings\\\" conflicts with a Table 2 footnote saying Grettefoss opened on 3 November. (3) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article as not relevant, while Table 3 and Section 4.1 show a coder disagreement on it. (4) It is unclear whether the 96 articles and 44 projects double-count the pilot (cannot_verify). (5) The Appendix A.3.2 precedence rule conflicts with its own bysykkelstativ example. (6) Figure 2 colours sykkelmulighet as Leisure although no Table 9 Leisure word part matches. Findings 5 and 6 affect the category shares in Table 8 by an unquantifiable amount.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"NUM-001\",\"category\":\"unit_denominator_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The 'about 6 percent' yield divides 2 distinct openings by 34 articles, but the paper's own counts show 5 of the 34 articles concern those openings (3 if the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded), so the sentence 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles ... concern an opening' mixes projects and articles.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 3.1.4 states that of the five relevant articles only two unique openings were found, with four articles on Homborsund and one on Stod. Table 2 shows 4 articles for Homborsund and 1 for Stod, and Figure 1 shows 5 articles coded relevant (15% of 34). The numerator '2' therefore counts distinct openings while the denominator '34' counts articles. The article-level share is 5/34 = 14.7%, or 3/34 = 8.8% if the two Homborsund articles published before the opening are excluded as in Section 4. The Figure 1 caption ('Only 2 of 70 search hits') uses the same project-over-hits ratio. This is a unit and denominator mismatch, not a rounding issue, and it understates the article-level yield used to argue that keyword search is too noisy. The abstract's 'only two actual openings' is a project-level count and is not itself affected.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text, Section 3.1.2\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim sentence on page 4.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text, Section 3.1.4\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim; Table 2 rows (4 and 1 articles) on the same page agree.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text, Figure 1 caption\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 / Figure 1\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Caption wording uses the same project-over-hits ratio.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"2 of 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"The paper's own article counts give 5 (or 3) of 34, not 2.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"arithmetic\",\"operation\":\"ratio\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"5\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Articles concerning the two openings: four on Homborsund plus one on Stod\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"34\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"pilot sample, unique articles after removing 36 duplicates\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Denominator stated in the sentence\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"reported\":{\"value\":\"6\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"percent of unique articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"'about 6 percent' in the text, which equals 2/34 = 5.9%\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.5\",\"scale\":\"percent\"},\"computed_value\":\"14.7\",\"tolerance\":\"0.5 percentage points\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Stated 6% (2 openings / 34 articles) versus 14.7% (5 articles / 34 articles) at article level, or 8.8% (3/34) if the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The authors may intend a project-level yield but divided distinct projects by an article count, which mixes units.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"Report the article-level share (5 of 34, or 3 of 34 under the Section 4 coding) and the project-level count (2 openings) separately with matching denominators, or define the yield explicitly as openings per unique article.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Rewrite the sentence and Figure 1 caption so that numerator and denominator use the same unit: either '5 of the 34 unique articles (15 percent) report an opening that took place, covering 2 distinct openings', or a project-level ratio with a project-level denominator.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-002\",\"category\":\"count_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The paper reports only two openings that actually took place (Figure 1 caption, abstract), but Table 2 footnote c says Grettefoss Bridge was confirmed to have opened on 3 November 2026, before the 9 November paper date, while Table 2 still lists its status as 'Planned'.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4 / Table 2\",\"text_quote\":\"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening that actually took place (Homborsund and Stod/Steinkjer); the two other articles describe planned openings.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Figure 1 and the abstract count two openings that took place. Table 2 footnote c says the Grettefoss opening was 'Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.' The Tromsø opening, by contrast, was delayed to 27 November as of 6 November. The paper's own coding rule says planned openings should be recorded and checked for whether the date has passed. Table 2 labels Grettefoss 'Planned' in the Status column, so the status and the footnote point in different directions. The two counts may be dated differently (status at article publication versus status when the paper was written), but the paper does not say so, and the headline count and the Table 2 status column do not match the footnote.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text, Figure 1 caption\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 / Figure 1\",\"text_quote\":\"Two further articles describe planned openings (Tromsø Bridge and Grettefoss Bridge), coded as “unclear”.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim caption text.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text, Table 2 row\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"Table 2\",\"text_quote\":\"Grettefoss Bridge Flesberg 1 3 Nov 2026c Planned\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Page text used because table_2.md omits this row (parser quality guidance).\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text, Table 2 footnote c\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"Table 2\",\"text_quote\":\"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote marker 'c' is attached to 'Confirmed' in extraction; quote is the substring after the marker.\"},{\"id\":\"S4\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 1 text, abstract\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_001.md\",\"page\":1,\"page_label\":\"1\",\"section\":\"Abstract\",\"text_quote\":\"contained only two actual openings\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-ae6010b8e427194ea28d441e\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Abstract statement of the same count.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"The pilot contained only two actual openings\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\",\"S4\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Count holds only as of article publication; the Table 2 footnote implies a third opening had occurred by the paper date.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"openings that took place\",\"sample\":\"pilot: 70 search hits, 34 unique articles\",\"denominator\":\"70 search hits / 34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Figure 1 caption and abstract count of actual openings\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"3 November 2026\",\"source_id\":\"S3\",\"unit\":\"confirmed opening date of Grettefoss Bridge\",\"sample\":\"Grettefoss Bridge project (1 article)\",\"denominator\":\"single project\",\"context\":\"Table 2 footnote c, status confirmed after publication\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Both refer to the same pilot sample. The headline count appears to be as of article publication, while footnote c is a later update (Tromsø's update is dated 6 November); the reference dates are not stated to match.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Two openings are reported as having taken place, but the footnote implies Homborsund (5 Oct), Stod (1 Sep) and Grettefoss (3 Nov), which is three by 9 November 2026. The Status column still reads 'Planned' for Grettefoss.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The count and status may be frozen at article publication while the footnotes record later follow-up.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State the reference date for the count and the status column, and either update the count and status to 3 or say explicitly that the count is as of article publication; reconcile the 6 percent yield accordingly.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State the as-of date for the opening count and the Status column. Reconcile Grettefoss's 'Planned' status with footnote c, and say whether the abstract's two openings and the yield figure should be updated to three.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-003\",\"category\":\"cross_source_count\",\"finding_summary\":\"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded 'not relevant by both human coders', but Section 4.1 and Table 3 show the Stord article is the one article on which the two coders disagreed, so one coder coded it relevant.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The Stord project appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Section 4.1 says the two coders agree on 33 of 34 articles. It says the only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County. Table 3 (rows = pilot coder, columns = second coder, with 3 relevant by the pilot coder and 4 by the second) shows one article coded not relevant by the pilot coder and relevant by the second coder. At least one human coder therefore did not code the Stord article as not relevant, which contradicts the footnote. The footnote is also used to justify counting Stord as a 44th project.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text, footnote 3\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim, though the footnote number is attached to 'The 96 articles' in the first sentence.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text, Section 4.1\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1\",\"text_quote\":\"The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County over a pedestrian crossing.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text, Table 3 row\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"Table 3\",\"text_quote\":\"Not relevant 1 30 31\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 3 body cells match table_3.png per the parser-quality review; header orientation (rows = pilot coder, columns = second coder) taken from the page text.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Stord article coded not relevant by both coders\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Table 3 and Section 4.1 show one coder coded it relevant.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"human coders coding the Stord article as not relevant\",\"sample\":\"Stord article in pilot\",\"denominator\":\"2 human coders\",\"context\":\"Footnote 3: both coders coded it not relevant\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"1\",\"source_id\":\"S3\",\"unit\":\"articles coded not relevant by the pilot coder and relevant by the second coder\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Off-diagonal cell in Table 3; Section 4.1 says this is the Stord article\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Same 34 pilot articles and same two human coders. The relevance coding treats 'unclear' as not relevant in both places.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"The footnote implies zero human-coder disagreements on Stord, whereas Table 3 and Section 4.1 report exactly one disagreement, on Stord.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The footnote may refer to a different coding stage or to the pre-opening rule, or the Table 3 orientation may differ from the footnote's assumption.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"Reconcile the footnote with Table 3 and say which coder or coders coded Stord as relevant.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Correct footnote 3 to describe how each human coder and the LLM coded the Stord article, consistent with Tables 3 and 4, and explain why a project coded not relevant by one or both humans counts among the 44 projects reporting an opening.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-004\",\"category\":\"aggregation_reconciliation\",\"finding_summary\":\"The 96 articles and 44 projects add 4 pilot articles and 1 pilot-only project to the 92 articles and 43 projects from rounds 2–4, but the paper does not say whether the pilot articles (2 Sep–10 Oct 2026) also appear in the 3,187-article run (October 2025–October 2026), so double-counting cannot be ruled out.\",\"issue_type\":\"cannot_verify\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"low\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44 unique projects.\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"The retained text does not say whether the pilot articles overlap the rounds 2–4 article set, or whether the Homborsund and Stod projects are among the 43 projects already counted.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"Footnote 3 states 96 = 92 (rounds 2–4) + 4 (pilot run) and 44 = 43 + Stord, which implies that Homborsund and Stod are already among the 43. The pilot sample was drawn between 2 Sep and 10 Oct 2026, and rounds 2–4 cover articles published between October 2025 and October 2026. Table 5 cites Homborsund articles dated 5 and 7 Oct 2026, which fall within both windows. If the pilot articles are disjoint from rounds 2–4, a separate set of Homborsund and Stod articles must sit in rounds 2–4. If they overlap, 96 double-counts articles. The arithmetic 92+4 = 96 is correct, but its validity depends on the unstated overlap.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text, Section 6 opening\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6\",\"text_quote\":\"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim; sentence wraps over two lines.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 text, footnote 3\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 / footnote 3\",\"text_quote\":\"articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote number attached to 'The 96 articles'; quote is the following substring.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 9 text, Section 5\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md\",\"page\":9,\"page_label\":\"9\",\"section\":\"5 Results\",\"text_quote\":\"The LLM coded 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4, published between October 2025 and October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim.\"},{\"id\":\"S4\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text, Section 3.1.2\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"96 articles and 44 projects are distinct counts across pilot and rounds 2–4\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\",\"S4\"],\"relation\":\"cannot_verify\",\"note\":\"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 is not stated.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Are the 4 pilot LLM-relevant articles and the Homborsund and Stod projects disjoint from the 92 articles and 43 projects of rounds 2–4, so that 92+4 = 96 and 43+1 = 44 count distinct units?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"92\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"rounds 2–4 LLM-relevant articles\",\"denominator\":\"3,187 articles coded\",\"context\":\"Rounds 2–4 relevant articles\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"4\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"pilot LLM-relevant articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 pilot articles\",\"context\":\"Pilot-run articles added in footnote 3\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"96\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"pilot plus rounds 2–4\",\"denominator\":\"not stated\",\"context\":\"Reported total\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Whether the pilot articles (2 Sep–10 Oct 2026) are included in the 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4\",\"Whether Homborsund and Stod are among the 43 projects found in rounds 2–4, and via which articles\",\"Article-level deduplication rule applied across rounds\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State whether the pilot sample is part of or disjoint from rounds 2–4, how overlapping articles were deduplicated across rounds, and which articles support Homborsund and Stod in rounds 2–4.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-005\",\"category\":\"definition_conflict\",\"finding_summary\":\"The Appendix A.3.2 rule that a word fitting several types takes the first type in Table 9 conflicts with its own example: bysykkelstativ contains 'stativ' (Parking & storage, listed before Infrastructure) yet is counted as infrastructure, and Figure 2 colours it as Infrastructure.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2 / Table 9\",\"text_quote\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table; words containing “bysykkel”, such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 9 lists Parking & storage (word parts include “stativ”) before Infrastructure (which includes “bysykkel”). The paper states the first-listed type applies when a word fits several types. For bysykkelstativ the first match would therefore be Parking & storage, yet the text and Figure 2 (blue, Infrastructure) put it in Infrastructure. Table 9 also lists “syklende” as Infrastructure although it contains the Proximity word part “sykle”, which comes earlier. The paper's explicit word-level assignments may override the stated rule, but this is not said. The classification feeds the category shares in Table 8 (Infrastructure 13.4%, Parking & storage 10.8%), and the size of the effect cannot be computed from the retained evidence.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text, A.3.2 rule and example\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2\",\"text_quote\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim; the example 'bysykkelstativ ... counted as infrastructure' follows.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text, Table 9 Parking & storage row\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"Table 9\",\"text_quote\":\"“stativ” (rack)\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 9 page text used, since the structured table is a single unstructured column per parser-quality guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"page 16 image, Figure 2\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/page_images/page_016.png\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":null,\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-aa2dd9d8124f250c7c1bf3e4\",\"correspondence\":\"visual\",\"verification_note\":\"Inspected the Figure 2 bars and legend: bysykkelstativ (0.5%) is blue, the Infrastructure colour. Bar colours were read visually.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"First type in Table 9 order applies; bysykkelstativ is infrastructure\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"By the stated precedence, 'stativ' (Parking & storage) would be matched before Infrastructure.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"How much of the Infrastructure share (13.4%) and the Parking & storage share (10.8%) in Table 8 depends on the stated precedence rule versus the word-level assignments actually used?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"0.5\",\"source_id\":\"S3\",\"unit\":\"percent of all listings\",\"sample\":\"700 579 listings, Jan 2020–Oct 2026\",\"denominator\":\"700 579 listings\",\"context\":\"Figure 2 bar for bysykkelstativ, coloured as Infrastructure\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.05\",\"scale\":\"percent\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Which classification rule the code actually applied (first-listed type versus explicit word lists)\",\"Listing counts for words whose type depends on the precedence rule\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State the actual precedence used in the classification code and make the example consistent with it, or reorder Table 9. Say which of the Table 8 category shares change under the alternative rule.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-006\",\"category\":\"definition_conflict\",\"finding_summary\":\"Figure 2 colours 'sykkelmulighet' as Leisure, but none of the Leisure word parts in Table 9 appears in it (sykling, syklist, terreng, løype, klubb, miljø, område), and Table 9 says all remaining words are Other.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":\"sykkelmulighet (cycling opportunities) 0.3%\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Colours in Figure 2 indicate the category of each word according to the Table 9 classification rule.\",\"assessment\":\"partially\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"In the Figure 2 image, sykkelmulighet (0.3%) is drawn in the pink Leisure colour per the legend. The Leisure row of Table 9 lists the word parts “sykling”, “syklist”, “terreng”, “løype”, “klubb”, “miljø” and “område”. 'sykkelmulighet' contains none of them, and no other category's word part obviously matches it either, so under the stated rule it would fall in Other. Other word-to-colour assignments in Figure 2 appear consistent with Table 9. Because the Leisure share in Table 8 (3.8%) is a union over many words, the effect on it cannot be computed from the retained evidence.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"page 16 image, Figure 2\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/page_images/page_016.png\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":null,\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-aa2dd9d8124f250c7c1bf3e4\",\"correspondence\":\"visual\",\"verification_note\":\"Inspected the sykkelmulighet bar and the legend: pink bar matches the Leisure swatch. Substring matching against Table 9 word parts was done manually.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 16 text, Figure 2 labels\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":\"sykkelmulighet (cycling opportunities) 0.3%\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Bar label and value read verbatim from page text.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text, Table 9 Leisure row\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"Table 9\",\"text_quote\":\"Leisure “sykling” (cycling), “syklist” (cyclist), “terreng” (terrain), “løype” (trail),\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Verbatim from page text; the structured table file is unreliable per parser-quality guidance.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Word colours follow the Table 9 classification\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"sykkelmulighet is coloured Leisure although no Leisure word part matches.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Is sykkelmulighet (0.3% of listings) classified as Leisure or Other in the data underlying Table 8, and how large is the resulting change in the Leisure (3.8%) and Other (1.0%) shares?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"0.3\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"percent of all listings\",\"sample\":\"700 579 listings, Jan 2020–Oct 2026\",\"denominator\":\"700 579 listings\",\"context\":\"Figure 2 bar for sykkelmulighet\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.05\",\"scale\":\"percent\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Actual classification applied to sykkelmulighet\",\"Overlap of sykkelmulighet listings with other Leisure or Other words\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Clarify whether sykkelmulighet was deliberately coded as Leisure, add the corresponding word part to Table 9, or recolour it as Other.\"}],\"notes\":[\"Parser-quality guidance was respected: structured table CSV/markdown files were not used as primary evidence. Page-level text and page images were used for Tables 1–9 and Figures 1–4.\",\"The full manuscript text (full_text.md, pages 1–18) was read in full and every numeric claim in the body, tables, figure captions and appendix was checked. numbers_in_text.json (about 161 kB) was read only for its first 150 lines (page 1), because it is a context index of the same text; the systematic pass relied on full_text.md.\",\"Arithmetic was done by hand. The scripts/numerical_checks.py wrapper was not run (no shell tool), so none of the recomputations was run through the wrapper.\",\"Reconciliations that passed: 70−36 = 34; 34/70 = 48.6% (49%); 5/34 = 14.7% (15%); 5+8+21 = 34; 3/34 relevant; Tables 3 and 4 totals and 33/34 = 97.06%; 1/34 = 2.9% LLM run disagreement; Table 6 date-precision 19+10+9+5 = 43 and Day+Month = 29; 44−18 = 26 and 17+2 = 19 day-dated, equal to Table 6's 19 if Stord is not day-dated; Table 8 counts sum to 700,579 and every share recomputes; 266,625/700,579 = 38.1%; 4 Sep → 5 Oct 2026 ≈ one month; 5 Oct 2026 is a Monday; 35%→44% ≈ 9 pp matches Figure 3; county percentages in the text match the Figure 4 labels.\",\"Items judged rounding-compatible or too minor to report: Table 5 length 2,132 m versus road-link ranges 1492+641 = 2133 m (1 m, within rounding); Section 6.2's 'between a third and a half' versus counts of 15–24 of 44 (34%–55%, loose wording); Section A.2 'first quarter of 2024 is missing' versus a Jan–April 2024 gap (Figure 3 shows no Q1 point and a Q2 2024 point that is partly affected).\",\"Not verifiable from retained artifacts: external figures cited from the literature (Copenhagen +60% trips, Fyhri up to 5 pp, Bartik 96% accuracy), and the Figure 4 dashed Norway line (the page-17 image was not viewed; only the bar labels from page text were checked).\"],\"completion\":{\"version\":1,\"state\":\"complete\",\"scope_description\":\"Numerical audit of work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed: all numeric statements in the abstract, body, Tables 1–9, Figures 1–4, footnotes and Appendix A. Checks covered recomputation of counts, shares and percent/percentage-point statements, accounting identities (funnel, 2×2 tables, date-precision totals, project splits, listing shares), unit and denominator consistency, and text-versus-display agreement.\",\"checks_completed\":[\"Read parser_quality_auditor guidance and used page text and page images in place of unreliable structured table files\",\"Read full_text.md pages 1–18 in full and recomputed every material numeric sentence\",\"Pilot funnel: 70/36/34, 5/8/21 coding split, percent-retained labels, 2-of-34 yield (found unit mismatch)\",\"Table 2 and Figure 1 opening counts versus footnotes\",\"Tables 3 and 4: totals, 33/34 agreement, Stord disagreement, footnote 3 consistency\",\"Table 5: dates, elapsed month, weekday, length sum, gradient and elevation entries\",\"Table 6 and Section 5: 92, 43, 50, 236, 29, 14 of 15 counties, date-precision adding-up\",\"Section 6 and Table 7: 96 and 44 reconciliation, 42/44, 18+26, 17+2\",\"Appendix A: Table 8 share recomputation, additivity note, Figure 2 versus Table 8 bounds, Figure 2 colours versus Table 9 rules, Figure 3 reading versus 35%→44% and 9 pp, Figure 4 labels versus text\",\"Read the first 150 lines of numbers_in_text.json\"],\"missing_checks\":[],\"evidence_limitations\":[\"Arithmetic was done by hand; the scripts/numerical_checks.py wrapper was not run.\",\"numbers_in_text.json was read only in part; the systematic pass relied on full_text.md.\",\"The page-17 image and the Figure 4 dashed line were not visually inspected.\",\"External literature figures were not retrieved or verified.\",\"Figure 2 and Figure 3 values were read from page text and the page-16 image; no underlying data were available.\",\"Whether the pilot overlaps the rounds 2–4 article set is not recoverable from the retained evidence (NUM-004).\"]},\"coverage\":[{\"item_id\":\"assigned_remit\",\"source_object_ids\":[],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Systematic numerical pass over full_text.md (pages 1–18), all tables and figures via page text and images, plus the first 150 lines of numbers_in_text.json.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Six issues found (NUM-001 to NUM-006). All other recomputed identities and text-versus-display comparisons reconciled or were rounding-compatible. The wrapper script was not run; arithmetic was by hand.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\",\"NUM-002\",\"NUM-003\",\"NUM-004\",\"NUM-005\",\"NUM-006\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"sampled\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Used the Figure 1 caption and page-4 text (the crop omits the chart); verified 70, 34, 49%, 5, 15%, 2 and the 6 percent statement.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The funnel numbers reconcile, but the article-versus-project unit in 2/34 and the two-opening count are defective (NUM-001, NUM-002).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\",\"NUM-002\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Compared Figure 2 labels in page-16 text and the page image with Table 8 and Table 9; checked that category shares are at least the largest member word and at most the sum of member words.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Bar values and share bounds are consistent with Table 8; the colour and classification conflicts are NUM-005 and NUM-006.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-005\",\"NUM-006\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\"],\"claim\":\"The share mentioning cycling rose from about 35 percent in 2020 to about 44 percent at the end of the period, about 9 percentage points.\",\"check_performed\":\"Read the Figure 3 series on the page-16 image (about 35% in early 2020, about 44% at the end, dip in late 2023, gap in 2024) and subtracted.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The image supports 35% to 44% (+9 pp) and the late-2023 dip. The Q1-versus-January–April wording nuance was judged too minor to report. The axis text is scrambled in the page text, so the image was used.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\"],\"claim\":\"Cycling is mentioned in 61% (Oslo), 52% (Akershus), 38% (Norway); lowest are 14, 13 and 7 percent in Telemark, Nordland and Møre og Romsdal.\",\"check_performed\":\"Compared the Figure 4 bar labels in page-17 text with the text percentages and rounding.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All 15 county values round to the stated figures and the three lowest are correctly identified. The dashed Norway line was not visually inspected, so the 38% line position is unverified.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"sampled\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 1 from page-5 text; no quantities besides illustrative pilot examples (3 km, 3.5 m, 4 articles in 2 newspapers).\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Table 1 is a categorical inventory; the Homborsund 4-articles example matches Table 2. No defect found.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\"],\"claim\":\"Table 2 lists the pilot's events: two opened, two planned.\",\"check_performed\":\"Used page-5 text (the structured table is truncated); summed articles 4+1+1+1 = 7 = 5 relevant + 2 planned; compared statuses and footnotes with the Figure 1 caption.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Article counts reconcile, but the Grettefoss status 'Planned' conflicts with footnote c and the two-opening headline (NUM-002).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-002\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\"],\"claim\":\"Pilot coder and second coder agree on 33 of 34 articles (97%).\",\"check_performed\":\"Verified cell and margin sums (3+0=3, 1+30=31, 3+1=4, 0+30=30, total 34), 33/34 = 97.06%, and the Stord statement against footnote 3.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Table arithmetic is correct. Footnote 3's claim that both coders coded Stord not relevant conflicts with Table 3 (NUM-003).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-003\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\"],\"claim\":\"Pilot coder and LLM agree on 97% (33 of 34); LLM dates match in all three.\",\"check_performed\":\"Verified sums and 33/34 = 97.06%; compared with the abstract, Section 3.2 (1 of 34 = 2.9% run disagreement) and the 4 LLM-relevant articles used in footnote 3.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Arithmetic and text agree. The 4 LLM-relevant total feeds the NUM-004 reconciliation question, which is reported separately.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf-placeholder-unused\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\"],\"claim\":\"Table 5: the Homborsund path opened on 5 October 2026, NVDB geometry was registered 4 September 2026 (one month earlier), length 2,132 m.\",\"check_performed\":\"Checked the elapsed time (31 days), the weekday (5 Oct 2026 is a Monday), the length versus road-link ranges (1492+641 = 2133 m), and the gradient and elevation entries.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"The 1 m difference in length is rounding-compatible, and the other entries are internally consistent. The structured table is mis-columned, so the page text was used.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\"],\"claim\":\"Table 5 NVDB values are consistent with the text (one month before the opening; exact date added by articles).\",\"check_performed\":\"Compared Table 5 page text with the Section 4.3 narrative and note.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"No numerical conflict found between table, note and narrative.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\"],\"claim\":\"3,187 articles coded; 92 relevant; 43 projects; 29 dated to day or month; 14 of 15 counties.\",\"check_performed\":\"Verified 19+10+9+5 = 43, 19+10 = 29, 50 outlets of 236, and the county count against the 15 counties in Figure 4.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All adding-up identities hold and the text matches Table 6. The structured file is interleaved, so the page text and image were used.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\"],\"claim\":\"Of the 44 projects, almost all have location descriptions and between a third and a half contain most other groups.\",\"check_performed\":\"Read counts from page-11 text and computed shares (42/44 = 95%; 15–24 of 44 = 34%–55%); checked 18+26 = 44 and 17+2 = 19 against Table 6.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Counts agree with the text, apart from loose wording (24/44 is slightly above half) that was judged too minor to report. The 96/44 reconciliation is reported separately as NUM-004.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\"],\"claim\":\"266 625 of 700 579 listings (38.1%) mention cycling; type shares 13.4%, 10.8%, 10.7%, 9.8%, 3.8%, 1.0%.\",\"check_performed\":\"Used page-15 text (the structured table splits thousands): 266,625+433,954 = 700,579; recomputed all eight shares to 1 decimal; checked the non-additivity note; compared 9.8% with Figure 2 and the text percentages.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All counts and shares recompute within rounding, and the non-additive type rows are explained by the note. Only the classification-rule conflicts are reported (NUM-005, NUM-006).\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\"],\"claim\":\"Words are assigned to the first matching type in Table 9; bysykkelstativ is infrastructure.\",\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 9 from page-18 text and tested the precedence rule and example against the word parts; checked Figure 2 word colours against the table.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"The precedence rule conflicts with its own example, and sykkelmulighet is coloured Leisure without a matching word part.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-005\",\"NUM-006\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"claim:abstract-and-intro-headline-numbers\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-ae6010b8e427194ea28d441e\",\"OBJ-c45862491200db070adbb6ed\"],\"claim\":\"Abstract and introduction: 97 percent agreement, 3,187 articles, 92 openings, 43 projects, 29 dated to day or month, 14 of 15 counties, 700 579 listings, 38 percent mention cycling.\",\"check_performed\":\"Compared each headline number with Tables 3–4, 6 and 8 and the body text.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All headline figures agree with the tables and body text; the only issue is the two-opening count (NUM-002), reported separately.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"claim:external-literature-numbers\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-c45862491200db070adbb6ed\"],\"claim\":\"Copenhagen bicycle trips rose 60 percent; Fyhri et al. find up to five percentage points; Bartik et al. reach 96 percent accuracy.\",\"check_performed\":\"Identified these cited external figures; no retrieval was attempted.\",\"status\":\"cannot_verify\",\"reason\":\"These figures depend on external papers that are not retained in the parsed artifacts and were not retrieved; they sit outside the paper's own numerical results.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":false,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"sampled\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer":"numerical_auditor","paper_id":"bicycle-infrastructure-paper","run_status":"ok","summary":"Most headline numbers reconcile: the 70→36 duplicates→34 pilot funnel, the 5/8/21 coding split, the 2×2 agreement tables (33/34 = 97.1%), Table 6 (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the 44-project split (18+26), and the Table 8 listing shares (counts sum to 700,579; all shares recompute). The 35%→44% rise (about 9 pp) matches Figure 3, and the county shares in the text match Figure 4. Six defects remain. (1) The \"2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent)\" yield divides distinct openings by articles, while the paper's own counts give 5 articles. (2) \"Only two actual openings\" conflicts with a Table 2 footnote saying Grettefoss opened on 3 November. (3) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article as not relevant, while Table 3 and Section 4.1 show a coder disagreement on it. (4) It is unclear whether the 96 articles and 44 projects double-count the pilot (cannot_verify). (5) The Appendix A.3.2 precedence rule conflicts with its own bysykkelstativ example. (6) Figure 2 colours sykkelmulighet as Leisure although no Table 9 Leisure word part matches. Findings 5 and 6 affect the category shares in Table 8 by an unquantifiable amount.","findings":[{"id":"NUM-001","category":"unit_denominator_mismatch","finding_summary":"The 'about 6 percent' yield divides 2 distinct openings by 34 articles, but the paper's own counts show 5 of the 34 articles concern those openings (3 if the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded), so the sentence 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles ... concern an opening' mixes projects and articles.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Pilot sample","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 3.1.4 states that of the five relevant articles only two unique openings were found, with four articles on Homborsund and one on Stod. Table 2 shows 4 articles for Homborsund and 1 for Stod, and Figure 1 shows 5 articles coded relevant (15% of 34). The numerator '2' therefore counts distinct openings while the denominator '34' counts articles. The article-level share is 5/34 = 14.7%, or 3/34 = 8.8% if the two Homborsund articles published before the opening are excluded as in Section 4. The Figure 1 caption ('Only 2 of 70 search hits') uses the same project-over-hits ratio. This is a unit and denominator mismatch, not a rounding issue, and it understates the article-level yield used to argue that keyword search is too noisy. The abstract's 'only two actual openings' is a project-level count and is not itself affected.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text, Section 3.1.2","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim sentence on page 4."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 5 text, Section 3.1.4","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found. Four of the articles mention Homborsund and one Stod.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim; Table 2 rows (4 and 1 articles) on the same page agree."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 4 text, Figure 1 caption","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 / Figure 1","text_quote":"Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Caption wording uses the same project-over-hits ratio."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"2 of 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"The paper's own article counts give 5 (or 3) of 34, not 2."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"arithmetic","operation":"ratio","quantities":[{"value":"5","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Articles concerning the two openings: four on Homborsund plus one on Stod","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"34","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"pilot sample, unique articles after removing 36 duplicates","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Denominator stated in the sentence","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"reported":{"value":"6","source_id":"S1","unit":"percent of unique articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"'about 6 percent' in the text, which equals 2/34 = 5.9%","rounding_half_width":"0.5","scale":"percent"},"computed_value":"14.7","tolerance":"0.5 percentage points","observed_discrepancy":"Stated 6% (2 openings / 34 articles) versus 14.7% (5 articles / 34 articles) at article level, or 8.8% (3/34) if the two pre-opening Homborsund articles are excluded.","possible_explanation":"The authors may intend a project-level yield but divided distinct projects by an article count, which mixes units.","suggested_correction":"Report the article-level share (5 of 34, or 3 of 34 under the Section 4 coding) and the project-level count (2 openings) separately with matching denominators, or define the yield explicitly as openings per unique article."},"suggested_fix":"Rewrite the sentence and Figure 1 caption so that numerator and denominator use the same unit: either '5 of the 34 unique articles (15 percent) report an opening that took place, covering 2 distinct openings', or a project-level ratio with a project-level denominator."},{"id":"NUM-002","category":"count_inconsistency","finding_summary":"The paper reports only two openings that actually took place (Figure 1 caption, abstract), but Table 2 footnote c says Grettefoss Bridge was confirmed to have opened on 3 November 2026, before the 9 November paper date, while Table 2 still lists its status as 'Planned'.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4 / Table 2","text_quote":"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening that actually took place (Homborsund and Stod/Steinkjer); the two other articles describe planned openings.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Figure 1 and the abstract count two openings that took place. Table 2 footnote c says the Grettefoss opening was 'Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.' The Tromsø opening, by contrast, was delayed to 27 November as of 6 November. The paper's own coding rule says planned openings should be recorded and checked for whether the date has passed. Table 2 labels Grettefoss 'Planned' in the Status column, so the status and the footnote point in different directions. The two counts may be dated differently (status at article publication versus status when the paper was written), but the paper does not say so, and the headline count and the Table 2 status column do not match the footnote.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text, Figure 1 caption","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 / Figure 1","text_quote":"Two further articles describe planned openings (Tromsø Bridge and Grettefoss Bridge), coded as “unclear”.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim caption text."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 5 text, Table 2 row","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"Table 2","text_quote":"Grettefoss Bridge Flesberg 1 3 Nov 2026c Planned","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Page text used because table_2.md omits this row (parser quality guidance)."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 5 text, Table 2 footnote c","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"Table 2","text_quote":"Confirmed to have opened 3 November as planned.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote marker 'c' is attached to 'Confirmed' in extraction; quote is the substring after the marker."},{"id":"S4","type":"text","label":"page 1 text, abstract","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_001.md","page":1,"page_label":"1","section":"Abstract","text_quote":"contained only two actual openings","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-ae6010b8e427194ea28d441e","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Abstract statement of the same count."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"The pilot contained only two actual openings","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3","S4"],"relation":"partial","note":"Count holds only as of article publication; the Table 2 footnote implies a third opening had occurred by the paper date."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"2","source_id":"S1","unit":"openings that took place","sample":"pilot: 70 search hits, 34 unique articles","denominator":"70 search hits / 34 unique articles","context":"Figure 1 caption and abstract count of actual openings","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"3 November 2026","source_id":"S3","unit":"confirmed opening date of Grettefoss Bridge","sample":"Grettefoss Bridge project (1 article)","denominator":"single project","context":"Table 2 footnote c, status confirmed after publication","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Both refer to the same pilot sample. The headline count appears to be as of article publication, while footnote c is a later update (Tromsø's update is dated 6 November); the reference dates are not stated to match.","observed_discrepancy":"Two openings are reported as having taken place, but the footnote implies Homborsund (5 Oct), Stod (1 Sep) and Grettefoss (3 Nov), which is three by 9 November 2026. The Status column still reads 'Planned' for Grettefoss.","possible_explanation":"The count and status may be frozen at article publication while the footnotes record later follow-up.","suggested_correction":"State the reference date for the count and the status column, and either update the count and status to 3 or say explicitly that the count is as of article publication; reconcile the 6 percent yield accordingly."},"suggested_fix":"State the as-of date for the opening count and the Status column. Reconcile Grettefoss's 'Planned' status with footnote c, and say whether the abstract's two openings and the yield figure should be updated to three."},{"id":"NUM-003","category":"cross_source_count","finding_summary":"Footnote 3 says the Stord project was coded 'not relevant by both human coders', but Section 4.1 and Table 3 show the Stord article is the one article on which the two coders disagreed, so one coder coded it relevant.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses / footnote 3","text_quote":"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The Stord project appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Section 4.1 says the two coders agree on 33 of 34 articles. It says the only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County. Table 3 (rows = pilot coder, columns = second coder, with 3 relevant by the pilot coder and 4 by the second) shows one article coded not relevant by the pilot coder and relevant by the second coder. At least one human coder therefore did not code the Stord article as not relevant, which contradicts the footnote. The footnote is also used to justify counting Stord as a 44th project.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text, footnote 3","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 / footnote 3","text_quote":"projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim, though the footnote number is attached to 'The 96 articles' in the first sentence."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 text, Section 4.1","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1","text_quote":"The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County over a pedestrian crossing.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 7 text, Table 3 row","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"Table 3","text_quote":"Not relevant 1 30 31","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 3 body cells match table_3.png per the parser-quality review; header orientation (rows = pilot coder, columns = second coder) taken from the page text."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Stord article coded not relevant by both coders","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"Table 3 and Section 4.1 show one coder coded it relevant."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"2","source_id":"S1","unit":"human coders coding the Stord article as not relevant","sample":"Stord article in pilot","denominator":"2 human coders","context":"Footnote 3: both coders coded it not relevant","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"1","source_id":"S3","unit":"articles coded not relevant by the pilot coder and relevant by the second coder","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Off-diagonal cell in Table 3; Section 4.1 says this is the Stord article","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Same 34 pilot articles and same two human coders. The relevance coding treats 'unclear' as not relevant in both places.","observed_discrepancy":"The footnote implies zero human-coder disagreements on Stord, whereas Table 3 and Section 4.1 report exactly one disagreement, on Stord.","possible_explanation":"The footnote may refer to a different coding stage or to the pre-opening rule, or the Table 3 orientation may differ from the footnote's assumption.","suggested_correction":"Reconcile the footnote with Table 3 and say which coder or coders coded Stord as relevant."},"suggested_fix":"Correct footnote 3 to describe how each human coder and the LLM coded the Stord article, consistent with Tables 3 and 4, and explain why a project coded not relevant by one or both humans counts among the 44 projects reporting an opening."},{"id":"NUM-004","category":"aggregation_reconciliation","finding_summary":"The 96 articles and 44 projects add 4 pilot articles and 1 pilot-only project to the 92 articles and 43 projects from rounds 2–4, but the paper does not say whether the pilot articles (2 Sep–10 Oct 2026) also appear in the 3,187-article run (October 2025–October 2026), so double-counting cannot be ruled out.","issue_type":"cannot_verify","severity":"low","confidence":"low","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 / footnote 3","text_quote":"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44 unique projects.","assessment":"cannot_verify","cannot_verify_reason":"The retained text does not say whether the pilot articles overlap the rounds 2–4 article set, or whether the Homborsund and Stod projects are among the 43 projects already counted.","evidence_summary":"Footnote 3 states 96 = 92 (rounds 2–4) + 4 (pilot run) and 44 = 43 + Stord, which implies that Homborsund and Stod are already among the 43. The pilot sample was drawn between 2 Sep and 10 Oct 2026, and rounds 2–4 cover articles published between October 2025 and October 2026. Table 5 cites Homborsund articles dated 5 and 7 Oct 2026, which fall within both windows. If the pilot articles are disjoint from rounds 2–4, a separate set of Homborsund and Stod articles must sit in rounds 2–4. If they overlap, 96 double-counts articles. The arithmetic 92+4 = 96 is correct, but its validity depends on the unstated overlap.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 text, Section 6 opening","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6","text_quote":"In total, 96 article records across the pilot and the later rounds reported an opening, resulting in 44","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim; sentence wraps over two lines."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 10 text, footnote 3","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 / footnote 3","text_quote":"articles consists of the 92 articles from rounds 2–4 (Section 5) and four from the pilot run","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote number attached to 'The 96 articles'; quote is the following substring."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 9 text, Section 5","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_009.md","page":9,"page_label":"9","section":"5 Results","text_quote":"The LLM coded 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4, published between October 2025 and October 2026","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-521bfe93a764059cd1136195","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim."},{"id":"S4","type":"text","label":"page 4 text, Section 3.1.2","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"A pilot sample of 70 search hits between 2 September and 10 October 2026","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"96 articles and 44 projects are distinct counts across pilot and rounds 2–4","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3","S4"],"relation":"cannot_verify","note":"Overlap between pilot and rounds 2–4 is not stated."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Are the 4 pilot LLM-relevant articles and the Homborsund and Stod projects disjoint from the 92 articles and 43 projects of rounds 2–4, so that 92+4 = 96 and 43+1 = 44 count distinct units?","quantities":[{"value":"92","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles","sample":"rounds 2–4 LLM-relevant articles","denominator":"3,187 articles coded","context":"Rounds 2–4 relevant articles","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"4","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles","sample":"pilot LLM-relevant articles","denominator":"34 pilot articles","context":"Pilot-run articles added in footnote 3","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"96","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles","sample":"pilot plus rounds 2–4","denominator":"not stated","context":"Reported total","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"missing_information":["Whether the pilot articles (2 Sep–10 Oct 2026) are included in the 3,187 articles from rounds 2–4","Whether Homborsund and Stod are among the 43 projects found in rounds 2–4, and via which articles","Article-level deduplication rule applied across rounds"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"State whether the pilot sample is part of or disjoint from rounds 2–4, how overlapping articles were deduplicated across rounds, and which articles support Homborsund and Stod in rounds 2–4."},{"id":"NUM-005","category":"definition_conflict","finding_summary":"The Appendix A.3.2 rule that a word fitting several types takes the first type in Table 9 conflicts with its own example: bysykkelstativ contains 'stativ' (Parking & storage, listed before Infrastructure) yet is counted as infrastructure, and Figure 2 colours it as Infrastructure.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2 / Table 9","text_quote":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table; words containing “bysykkel”, such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 9 lists Parking & storage (word parts include “stativ”) before Infrastructure (which includes “bysykkel”). The paper states the first-listed type applies when a word fits several types. For bysykkelstativ the first match would therefore be Parking & storage, yet the text and Figure 2 (blue, Infrastructure) put it in Infrastructure. Table 9 also lists “syklende” as Infrastructure although it contains the Proximity word part “sykle”, which comes earlier. The paper's explicit word-level assignments may override the stated rule, but this is not said. The classification feeds the category shares in Table 8 (Infrastructure 13.4%, Parking & storage 10.8%), and the size of the effect cannot be computed from the retained evidence.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 18 text, A.3.2 rule and example","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2","text_quote":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim; the example 'bysykkelstativ ... counted as infrastructure' follows."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 18 text, Table 9 Parking & storage row","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"Table 9","text_quote":"“stativ” (rack)","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 9 page text used, since the structured table is a single unstructured column per parser-quality guidance."},{"id":"S3","type":"figure","label":"page 16 image, Figure 2","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/page_images/page_016.png","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 2","text_quote":null,"url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-aa2dd9d8124f250c7c1bf3e4","correspondence":"visual","verification_note":"Inspected the Figure 2 bars and legend: bysykkelstativ (0.5%) is blue, the Infrastructure colour. Bar colours were read visually."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"First type in Table 9 order applies; bysykkelstativ is infrastructure","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"By the stated precedence, 'stativ' (Parking & storage) would be matched before Infrastructure."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"How much of the Infrastructure share (13.4%) and the Parking & storage share (10.8%) in Table 8 depends on the stated precedence rule versus the word-level assignments actually used?","quantities":[{"value":"0.5","source_id":"S3","unit":"percent of all listings","sample":"700 579 listings, Jan 2020–Oct 2026","denominator":"700 579 listings","context":"Figure 2 bar for bysykkelstativ, coloured as Infrastructure","rounding_half_width":"0.05","scale":"percent"}],"missing_information":["Which classification rule the code actually applied (first-listed type versus explicit word lists)","Listing counts for words whose type depends on the precedence rule"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"State the actual precedence used in the classification code and make the example consistent with it, or reorder Table 9. Say which of the Table 8 category shares change under the alternative rule."},{"id":"NUM-006","category":"definition_conflict","finding_summary":"Figure 2 colours 'sykkelmulighet' as Leisure, but none of the Leisure word parts in Table 9 appears in it (sykling, syklist, terreng, løype, klubb, miljø, område), and Table 9 says all remaining words are Other.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 2","text_quote":"sykkelmulighet (cycling opportunities) 0.3%","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Colours in Figure 2 indicate the category of each word according to the Table 9 classification rule.","assessment":"partially","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"In the Figure 2 image, sykkelmulighet (0.3%) is drawn in the pink Leisure colour per the legend. The Leisure row of Table 9 lists the word parts “sykling”, “syklist”, “terreng”, “løype”, “klubb”, “miljø” and “område”. 'sykkelmulighet' contains none of them, and no other category's word part obviously matches it either, so under the stated rule it would fall in Other. Other word-to-colour assignments in Figure 2 appear consistent with Table 9. Because the Leisure share in Table 8 (3.8%) is a union over many words, the effect on it cannot be computed from the retained evidence.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"figure","label":"page 16 image, Figure 2","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/page_images/page_016.png","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 2","text_quote":null,"url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-aa2dd9d8124f250c7c1bf3e4","correspondence":"visual","verification_note":"Inspected the sykkelmulighet bar and the legend: pink bar matches the Leisure swatch. Substring matching against Table 9 word parts was done manually."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 16 text, Figure 2 labels","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 2","text_quote":"sykkelmulighet (cycling opportunities) 0.3%","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Bar label and value read verbatim from page text."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 18 text, Table 9 Leisure row","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"Table 9","text_quote":"Leisure “sykling” (cycling), “syklist” (cyclist), “terreng” (terrain), “løype” (trail),","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Verbatim from page text; the structured table file is unreliable per parser-quality guidance."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Word colours follow the Table 9 classification","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"partial","note":"sykkelmulighet is coloured Leisure although no Leisure word part matches."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Is sykkelmulighet (0.3% of listings) classified as Leisure or Other in the data underlying Table 8, and how large is the resulting change in the Leisure (3.8%) and Other (1.0%) shares?","quantities":[{"value":"0.3","source_id":"S2","unit":"percent of all listings","sample":"700 579 listings, Jan 2020–Oct 2026","denominator":"700 579 listings","context":"Figure 2 bar for sykkelmulighet","rounding_half_width":"0.05","scale":"percent"}],"missing_information":["Actual classification applied to sykkelmulighet","Overlap of sykkelmulighet listings with other Leisure or Other words"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"Clarify whether sykkelmulighet was deliberately coded as Leisure, add the corresponding word part to Table 9, or recolour it as Other."}],"notes":["Parser-quality guidance was respected: structured table CSV/markdown files were not used as primary evidence. Page-level text and page images were used for Tables 1–9 and Figures 1–4.","The full manuscript text (full_text.md, pages 1–18) was read in full and every numeric claim in the body, tables, figure captions and appendix was checked. numbers_in_text.json (about 161 kB) was read only for its first 150 lines (page 1), because it is a context index of the same text; the systematic pass relied on full_text.md.","Arithmetic was done by hand. The scripts/numerical_checks.py wrapper was not run (no shell tool), so none of the recomputations was run through the wrapper.","Reconciliations that passed: 70−36 = 34; 34/70 = 48.6% (49%); 5/34 = 14.7% (15%); 5+8+21 = 34; 3/34 relevant; Tables 3 and 4 totals and 33/34 = 97.06%; 1/34 = 2.9% LLM run disagreement; Table 6 date-precision 19+10+9+5 = 43 and Day+Month = 29; 44−18 = 26 and 17+2 = 19 day-dated, equal to Table 6's 19 if Stord is not day-dated; Table 8 counts sum to 700,579 and every share recomputes; 266,625/700,579 = 38.1%; 4 Sep → 5 Oct 2026 ≈ one month; 5 Oct 2026 is a Monday; 35%→44% ≈ 9 pp matches Figure 3; county percentages in the text match the Figure 4 labels.","Items judged rounding-compatible or too minor to report: Table 5 length 2,132 m versus road-link ranges 1492+641 = 2133 m (1 m, within rounding); Section 6.2's 'between a third and a half' versus counts of 15–24 of 44 (34%–55%, loose wording); Section A.2 'first quarter of 2024 is missing' versus a Jan–April 2024 gap (Figure 3 shows no Q1 point and a Q2 2024 point that is partly affected).","Not verifiable from retained artifacts: external figures cited from the literature (Copenhagen +60% trips, Fyhri up to 5 pp, Bartik 96% accuracy), and the Figure 4 dashed Norway line (the page-17 image was not viewed; only the bar labels from page text were checked)."],"completion":{"version":1,"state":"complete","scope_description":"Numerical audit of work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed: all numeric statements in the abstract, body, Tables 1–9, Figures 1–4, footnotes and Appendix A. Checks covered recomputation of counts, shares and percent/percentage-point statements, accounting identities (funnel, 2×2 tables, date-precision totals, project splits, listing shares), unit and denominator consistency, and text-versus-display agreement.","checks_completed":["Read parser_quality_auditor guidance and used page text and page images in place of unreliable structured table files","Read full_text.md pages 1–18 in full and recomputed every material numeric sentence","Pilot funnel: 70/36/34, 5/8/21 coding split, percent-retained labels, 2-of-34 yield (found unit mismatch)","Table 2 and Figure 1 opening counts versus footnotes","Tables 3 and 4: totals, 33/34 agreement, Stord disagreement, footnote 3 consistency","Table 5: dates, elapsed month, we